   "Q3_NotApplicable": "Yes",
   "Q6_FollowUp": "No",
   "Q5_Strengths": "Responsive and clear communication: The Digital Hub team is very prompt in their communication and provides clear updates on requests and progress.\n\nTransparency around timelines: When the team is under pressure or managing competing priorities, they proactively communicate revised timelines and set clear expectations.\n\nWebsite support: They are particularly strong when it comes to website updates, demonstrating good responsiveness and an efficient approach to delivering requested changes.",
   "Q5_Improvements": "Internal alignment and ownership: There are occasions where technical requests shared with Digital Hub are redirected to another team, only for that team to subsequently advise that the work sits with Digital Hub. This creates unnecessary back-and-forth and delays. It would be beneficial for the teams to align internally on responsibilities and ownership before coming back to us, as we are not always across the internal team structures or technical responsibilities.\n\nTechnical knowledge and guidance: There is an opportunity for the technical team to demonstrate stronger technical understanding and provide more proactive guidance. Rather than simply redirecting requests or advising on what cannot be done, we'd value recommendations, best-practice advice and solutions that help us achieve the desired outcome.\n\nProactiveness and accountability: At times, the level of engagement and ownership from some technical team members can feel limited. Greater initiative, willingness to investigate issues and a more solution-oriented approach would help build confidence in the support provided and improve the overall working relationship.",
   "Q1_Function": "Marketing"
  },
